# Invoicing System — Clean-Slate Design

## Platform Context

Enforcer is an API marketplace. **Consumers** subscribe to plans. An invoice is generated when a consumer owes money.

| Flow | Scenarios | How |
|---|---|---|
| **Checkout UI (Custom)** | Subscribe, Plan Switch | Consumer previews invoice on our UI, pays via Stripe Elements PaymentIntent |
| **Direct Charge** | Renewal | Background job charges saved card, webhook confirms |

**Rule: An invoice is only persisted when payment is confirmed (for checkout flows) or just before a background charge (for renewals).**

---

## Checkout Flow (Subscribe + Plan Switch)

We are transitioning from Stripe Hosted Checkout to a Custom Checkout UI using Stripe Elements (PaymentIntents).

### 1. Preview Phase (No DB Mutation)
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Consumer
    participant API
    participant Factory as InvoiceFactory
    
    Consumer->>API: GET /api/billings/preview-subscription
    API->>API: Calculate promo, calculate wallet usage
    API->>Factory: ForSubscription / ForPlanSwitch → in-memory Invoice
    Factory-->>API: Invoice (NOT saved)
    API-->>Consumer: Returns InvoicePreviewResponse
```

### 2. Payment Phase (Total > 0)
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Consumer
    participant API
    participant Stripe
    participant Webhook
    participant DB

    Consumer->>API: POST /api/billings/payment-intent
    API->>API: Re-calculate totals securely
    API->>Stripe: Create PaymentIntent (amount, metadata)
    Stripe-->>Consumer: client_secret
    Consumer->>Stripe: Submit Stripe Payment Element

    Stripe->>Webhook: Checkout.Session.Completed / PaymentIntent.Succeeded
    Webhook->>API: Rebuild invoice from metadata
    Webhook->>DB: Save invoice
    Webhook->>DB: Redeem Promo & Charge Wallet
    Webhook->>DB: invoice.Pay()
    Webhook->>API: Create Subscription via ApiServices
```

### 3. Free Checkout Phase (Total = 0)
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Consumer
    participant API
    participant DB

    Consumer->>API: POST /api/billings/process-free-checkout
    API->>API: Re-calculate totals (Verify == 0)
    API->>API: Rebuild invoice
    API->>DB: Save invoice
    API->>DB: Redeem Promo & Charge Wallet
    API->>DB: invoice.Pay()
    API->>API: Create Subscription via ApiServices
    API-->>Consumer: Success
```

---

## Direct Charge Flow (Renewal)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Job as Background Job
    participant Factory as InvoiceFactory
    participant Stripe
    participant DB
    participant Webhook

    Job->>Factory: ForRenewal(subscription)
    Factory-->>Job: Invoice (in-memory)
    Job->>DB: Save invoice (Pending)
    Job->>Stripe: ChargeAsync(invoice) → creates PaymentIntent

    alt Payment succeeds
        Stripe->>Webhook: PaymentIntent.Succeeded
        Webhook->>Webhook: invoice.Pay()
        Webhook->>DB: Update invoice → Paid
    else Payment fails
        Stripe->>Webhook: PaymentIntent.Failed
        Webhook->>Webhook: invoice.RecordFailedAttempt()
        Webhook->>DB: Update invoice (still Pending, attempts++)
    end
```

> [!NOTE]
> For renewals, the invoice is saved **before** charging because there's no consumer interaction. The webhook then transitions it to [Paid](file:///c:/Users/Mhamed/source/repos/Backend%20Projects/enforcer/backend/src/Modules/Billings/Enforcer.Modules.Billings.Infrastructure/PaymentProcessing/StripeEvents/EventHandlers/PaymentIntentSucceededHandler.cs#52-64). If the charge fails, the webhook marks the attempt ([RecordFailedAttempt](file:///c:/Users/Mhamed/source/repos/Backend%20Projects/enforcer/backend/src/Modules/Billings/Enforcer.Modules.Billings.Domain/Invoices/Invoice.cs#97-98)).

---

## 1. Domain — Invoice Aggregate

### Invoice Entity

```csharp
public sealed class Invoice : Entity
{
    public Guid ConsumerId { get; private set; }
    public Guid? ReferenceId { get; private set; }  // generic link (subscription, order, etc.)
    public string InvoiceNumber { get; private set; }
    public string Currency { get; private set; }

    public long Subtotal { get; private set; }
    public long DiscountTotal { get; private set; }
    public long Total { get; private set; }

    public DateTime? PeriodStart { get; private set; }
    public DateTime? PeriodEnd { get; private set; }

    public InvoiceStatus Status { get; private set; }
    public DateTime IssuedAt { get; private set; }
    public DateTime? PaidAt { get; private set; }
    public int PaymentAttempts { get; private set; }
    public string? Notes { get; private set; }

    private List<LineItem> _lineItems;
    public IReadOnlyList<LineItem> LineItems => _lineItems;
}
```

### Construction — Born Complete, No `AddLineItem`

```csharp
public static Invoice Create(
    Guid consumerId, string currency, List<LineItem> lineItems,
    Guid? referenceId = null,
    DateTime? periodStart = null, DateTime? periodEnd = null,
    string? notes = null)
```

### Lifecycle

```csharp
public Result Pay()               // Pending → Paid
public Result Void()              // Pending → Void
public Result Refund(long amount) // Paid → Refunded | PartiallyRefunded
public void RecordFailedAttempt() // increments counter only
```

### Supporting Types

```csharp
public enum InvoiceStatus { Pending, Paid, Void, Refunded, PartiallyRefunded }
public enum LineItemType { Subscription, Overage, Credit, Discount, Fee, Tax }
```

